SearXNG
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Project:  https://github.com/searxng/searxng
    Licence:  AGPL-3.0-or-later
    Used as:  an unmodified upstream container image
              (searxng/searxng, pinned by digest in docker-compose.yml)

Veilix performs no search of its own. It sends queries to a SearXNG instance
over that instance's HTTP JSON API and presents the results.

How the two are combined:

  - SearXNG runs as a separate process in its own container.
  - The only interface between them is HTTP over a private Docker network.
  - No SearXNG source is copied, linked against, embedded, or modified. The
    image is used exactly as published upstream.
  - Configuration is supplied through a mounted settings.yml and environment
    variables, both of which are supported upstream inputs.

On this basis the Veilix source in this repository is distributed under the MIT
License. Anyone redistributing the combined system, or forking or patching
SearXNG itself, should evaluate their own obligations under the AGPL.

The full text of the AGPL-3.0 as it applies to SearXNG is published with that
project.

